From 862c02136090c61af5cab192743c73238d957f8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:11:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 51/70] CUDA/HIP: single-token MoE tail (down MUL_MAT_ID,
 expert weighting, residual ADD) in one MMVQ launch (GGML_HIP_MOE_DOWN_REDUCE)

The decode MoE FFN ended in three launches: the down MUL_MAT_ID (one block per row and
expert), moe_weighted_reduction and the residual ADD (bin_bcast). A new kernel computes
for a block of rows the dot products of every used expert (same lanes, blocks per lane,
warp combine and butterfly as the ncols_dst == 1 MMVQ kernel), weights them as
moe_weighted_reduction_f32 does (x0*w0, then fma per expert) and adds the residual, so the
result is bitwise that of the three kernels. The ADD may follow the reduction after views
or elided nodes (the next layer's state gather): it is written ahead of its position and
skipped there (ggml_backend_cuda_context::nodes_done_ahead); its output is checked not to
overlap any other input. New test-backend-ops case MOE_DOWN_REDUCE (Q5_K/Q6_K/Q4_K/Q8_0/
IQ4_XS, 2-8 experts); the kernel is taken for all of them.

LFM2.5-24B-A2B decode: 595 -> 521 kernels/token (2 per MoE layer).
llama-bench tg128 -r 5, 3 interleaved rounds, same binary env off/on:
4.817 -> 4.642 ms/token (207.6 -> 215.4 t/s). Greedy md5 equal (LFM plain);
test-backend-ops MOE_DOWN_REDUCE, MUL_MAT_ID pass.
